To represent a FEN (Florence Notation) of a chessboard in LATEX, you can use the `chessboard` package, which is a commonly recommended package for creating chess diagrams due to its flexibility and ease of use. It allows you to specify the initial position of the pieces directly using FEN.

Here's a simple example of how you can create a LATEX document to display a chessboard from a given FEN:

```latex
\documentclass{article}
\usepackage{chessboard}

\begin{document}

% FEN representation of a standard starting position
\chessboard[FEN="rnbqkbnr/pppppppp/8/8/8/8/PPPPPPPP/RNBQKBNR"]

% This represents a chessboard with all pieces in their starting positions

\end{document}
```

To compile this LATEX document, you'll need to use a LATEX distribution such as TeX Live, MiKTeX, or online compilers like Overleaf.

**Important Note**: The `chessboard` package is not included in all standard LATEX distributions. You may need to install it manually, especially if you're using MiKTeX.

