Here is a Java solution to determine if an integer `n` is a power of three without using loops or recursion:

```java
public class PowerOfThreeChecker {

    public static boolean isPowerOfThree(int n) {
        if (n <= 0) {
            return false; // 0 is not a positive power of three
        }

        int logResult = (int) Math.log(n); // Compute the base-3 logarithm
        return logResult == Math.log(n) / Math.log(3); // Check if it's an integer multiple of the base-3 log
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println(isPowerOfThree(27)); // Should print: true
        System.out.println(isPowerOfThree(0));    // Should print: false
        System.out.println(isPowerOfThree(-1));   // Should print: false
    }
}
```

